<div style="background:#fff;"><div class="cap-section"><div style="margin-bottom:8px;"><div style="margin-bottom:26px;"><h2 style="font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:28px;font-weight:600;color:var(--ink);line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:-0.02em;margin:0;">Frequently asked questions</h2></div>
    <div style="border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:var(--radius-card);overflow:hidden;background:#fff;">
      <details class="sc-faq" open>
      <summary>When should I choose flip chip over wire bond?<span class="sc-faq-mk">+</span></summary>
      <div class="sc-faq-a">Flip chip is well suited to applications that require higher I/O density, shorter electrical paths for RF or high-speed signals, or a lower assembly profile. The die is connected directly to the substrate through its bump array rather than through wire loops.</div>
    </details>
      <details class="sc-faq">
      <summary>What bump types and pitch do you handle?<span class="sc-faq-mk">+</span></summary>
      <div class="sc-faq-a">Hana supports C4 solder bumps and copper pillars with bump pitch down to 80 µm. Face-down placement is accurate to ±10 µm, with mass reflow or thermo-compression bonding selected according to the design.</div>
    </details>
      <details class="sc-faq">
      <summary>How is joint integrity verified?<span class="sc-faq-mk">+</span></summary>
      <div class="sc-faq-a">Joint arrays are inspected using 2D and 3D (CT) X-ray, together with underfill void and fillet inspection. AEC-Q and IPC reliability testing is also available in-house.</div>
    </details>
      <details class="sc-faq">
      <summary>What quality systems cover flip chip?<span class="sc-faq-mk">+</span></summary>
      <div class="sc-faq-a">ISO 9001 applies group-wide, with IATF 16949 on automotive lines and ISO 13485 for medical work. Assembly runs in ESD-controlled areas meeting ANSI/ESD S20.20.</div>
    </details>
      <details class="sc-faq">
      <summary>Do you protect customer designs and IP?<span class="sc-faq-mk">+</span></summary>
      <div class="sc-faq-a">An NDA is signed before die, bump-map or CAD files are shared. Build areas are access-controlled, and programs can be assigned to dedicated lines where required.</div>
    </details>
